            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>
                    Column A: To the Deified Poppaea Augusta, [wife] of Imperator Nero Caesar Augustus. Lucius Titinius Glaucus Lucretianus, son of Lucius, of tribe Galeria,
                    flamen of Roma and Augustus, duovir for the 4th time, patron of the colony, sevir of the Roman equites, curio, prefect of engineers for the consul,
                    military tribune of the 22nd Legion Primigenia, prefect for the legate of the Balearic Islands, military tribune of the 6th Legion Victrix, 
                    in accordance with a vow undertaken for the safety of Imperator Nero, which he undertook in the Balearic Islands, in the year that Aulus Licinius Nerva
                    was consul, and Lucius Saufeius Vegetus and Quintus Aburius Nepos were duovirs, when he wished to erect it, having had his vow granted, he erected it
                    to Jupiter, Juno, Minerva, the Felicitas of Roma, [and] the Divine Augustus.
                    Column b: To Imperator Nero Claudius Caesar Augustus Germanicus, son of the divine Claudius, grandson of Germanicus Caesar, great-grandson of Tiberius Caesar Augustus, 
                    great-great-grandson of the deified Augustus, pontifex maximus, bearer of the tribunician power for the 13th time, imperator 11 times, and consul 4. 
                    Lucius Titinius Glaucus Lucretianus, son of Lucius, of the tribe Galeria, flamen of Rome and Augustus, duovir for the 4th time, patron of the colony, sevir of the 
                    Roman equites, curio, prefect of engineers for the consul, military tribune of the 22nd Legion Primigenia, prefect for the legate of the Balearic Islands, military tribune
                    of the 6th Legion Victrix, in accordance with a vow undertaken for the safety of Imperator Nero, which he undertook in the Balaeric Islands, in the year that Aulus
                    Licinius Nerva was consul, and Lucius Saufeius Vegetus and Quintus Aburius Nepos were duovirs, when he wished to erect it, having had his vow granted, he erected it
                    to Jupiter, Juno, Minerva, the Felicitas of Roma, [and] the Divine Augustus.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div type="commentary">
                <p>This monument can be dated to 66 CE on the basis of Nero's titulature, with the vow having been made the year previously (65 CE) in the consulship of Aulus Licinius Nerva.
                    As Sherk (1988, 72 n.4) stresses, his co-consul, M. Vestinius Atticus, is not mentioned, likely due to the fact that Nero had ordered his death and he committed suicide
                    (Tac. Ann. 15.68–69) on the basis of his implication in Piso's plot against him. <!-- AUGUSTUS TO HADRIAN BOOK, NEEDS REFERENCE -->
                    This is the same Lucius Titinius Glaucus Lucretianus as in <ref target="EmpWor000477">EmpWor000477</ref> from Luna (It. VII), <ref target="EmpWor000475">EmpWor000475</ref> that is probably also from Luna (It. VII), and in CIL 11.1332 and CIL 11,1349a (both from Luna, It. VII). He may also be attested in <ref target="EmpWor000451">EmpWor000451</ref> from Cosa (It. VII).
                </p> 
            </div>
